<article> <header class="hero"> <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"> <a href="/">Home</a> <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="9 18 15 12 9 6"/></svg> <a href="/glossary">Glossary</a> <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="9 18 15 12 9 6"/></svg> <span>Structured address</span> </nav> <div class="hero-badge"><span class="pulse-dot"></span><span style="position:relative;z-index:1">Glossary · Formats</span></div> <h1><span class="accent">Structured address</span></h1> <p class="page-meta">Glossary entry · Last reviewed 26 July 2026</p> <!-- ANSWER BLOCK — picked up by speakable schema --> <p class="answer-block">A <strong>fully structured address</strong> carries every postal-address component in its dedicated ISO 20022 XML element — <code>&lt;StrtNm&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;BldgNb&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;PstCd&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;TwnNm&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;Ctry&gt;</code> and the other elements of the <code>&lt;PstlAdr&gt;</code> block — with <strong>no free-format <code>&lt;AdrLine&gt;</code> permitted</strong>. It is the preferred format under the CPMI harmonised data model and has no end date.</p> </header> <section class="section"> <div class="section-label">In Practice</div> <h2 class="section-title">How Structured address works in practice</h2> <div class="content-block"><p>Fully structured is the format regulators and schemes designate as the target state: it maximises STP and screening precision because every component is machine-addressable. <code>&lt;TwnNm&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;Ctry&gt;</code> remain mandatory, and the EPC recommends migrating straight from unstructured to fully structured rather than stopping at hybrid.</p></div> <p class="src">Source: the ioNova Postal Address Specification v2.0 §3.3 Table 5 / §7.1 Table 12; EPC 153-22 v2.1; the ioNova Postal Address Specification v2.0 §9 (EPC recommendation).</p> <div class="content-block"><p>A fully structured address (the campaign's worked example):</p></div>
<div class="code-block"><pre><span class="tag">&lt;PstlAdr&gt;</span>
  <span class="tag">&lt;StrtNm&gt;</span>CUBA STREET<span class="tag">&lt;/StrtNm&gt;</span>
  <span class="tag">&lt;BldgNb&gt;</span>169<span class="tag">&lt;/BldgNb&gt;</span>
  <span class="tag">&lt;PstCd&gt;</span>6011<span class="tag">&lt;/PstCd&gt;</span>
  <span class="tag">&lt;TwnNm&gt;</span>WELLINGTON<span class="tag">&lt;/TwnNm&gt;</span>
  <span class="tag">&lt;Ctry&gt;</span>NZ<span class="tag">&lt;/Ctry&gt;</span>
<span class="tag">&lt;/PstlAdr&gt;</span></pre></div> <div class="content-block"><p>Parent reference: <a href="/address-intelligence/structured-address-mandate">ISO 20022 structured address mandate</a>.</p></div> </section> <section class="section"> <div class="section-label">Citations</div> <h2 class="section-title">Sources</h2> <div class="sources-list"> <h3 class="sources-subhead">Standards &amp; regulatory sources</h3>
